.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_RATELIMIT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_new ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_free ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_allow ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_delay ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_consume ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_tokens ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_set_rate ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_set_burst ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_rate ,
.Nm mbt_ratelimit_burst
.Nd Token bucket rate limiter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/ratelimit.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_new "struct mbt_ratelimit **out" "uint64_t rate" "uint64_t burst"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_free "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_allow "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl" "size_t n"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_delay "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl" "size_t n"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_consume "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl" "size_t n"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_tokens "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_set_rate "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl" "uint64_t rate"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_set_burst "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl" "uint64_t burst"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_rate "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl"
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_burst "struct mbt_ratelimit *rl"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_ratelimit
library implements a token bucket rate limiter. Tokens
refill at the specified
.Vt rate
(bytes per second) up to a maximum of
.Vt burst
tokens. A transfer of
.Vt N
bytes requires
.Vt N
tokens. If the
.Nm mbt_ratelimit
rate is set to 0, the limiter allows unlimited transfers immediately.
.Pp
The following functions manage the lifetime and configuration:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_new
Creates a new rate limiter. Returns 0 on success or error code on failure.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_free
Destroys the rate limiter and frees its resources.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_set_rate
Updates the refill rate at runtime.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 8
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_set_burst
Updates the maximum burst size at runtime.
.El
.Sh RATE LIMITING OPERATIONS
The following functions perform rate-limited operations:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_allow
Attempts to consume
.Vt n
tokens immediately. If successful, returns
.Fa true
and consumes the tokens. If insufficient tokens are available, returns
.Fa false
and does not consume any tokens.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_delay
Returns the number of microseconds until
.Vt n
tokens become available. Returns 0 if enough tokens are currently available.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_consume
Unconditionally consumes
.Vt n
tokens. This should be called after a sufficient delay has elapsed, as reported by
.Fn mbt_ratelimit_delay.
.El
.Sh INSPECTION
The following functions allow inspecting the current state:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_tokens
Returns the number of tokens currently available in the bucket.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 8
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_rate
Returns the current refill rate in bytes per second.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 8
.It .Fn mbt_ratelimit_burst
Returns the current maximum burst size.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3
